This directory is admittedly a mess.  What you need to know is

1. Edit macros to get correctly defined functions 
EditAllFiles.pl should do all of the editing necessary to get this stuff to work.  For example to get this to work with the standard cuts just run
perl EditAllFiles.pl 15 100 30 60 | grep cp > rename.csh
[you can check that the file edits are sane at this step by looking at *.new]
csh rename.csh
EditAll.pl adds the lines needed to the macros.

2.  run combinedStandard.C
root combinedStandard.C'(3,true)'
root combinedStandard.C'(5,true)'
makes comparisonManyStandardCB10to20.C and comparisonManyStandardCB40to80.C
Note that to get this right you have to edit the number of trigger particles in each bin from the text file output

3.  Append codesnippet to the end of these files.  Now they calculate the systematic error for these bins.